    "text": "**Case A**\n\n- **A1 \u2013 Cannot tell.** The search covered only the past seven days, so earlier misuse outside that window is not ruled out. It is also not settled that the burst was misuse at all.\n- **A2 \u2013 Yes.** The burst (new proxy, new fingerprint, payout changes) happened at 19 minutes and the check scored at 30 minutes, so the signals existed when it ran. This assumes the platform's own check can see the platform's request and account events, which is not stated.\n- **A3 \u2013 No, not by itself.** A shared payout destination fits one owner, but it also fits a shared processor or a mule account used by several parties.\n- **A4 \u2013 Yes, weakly.** Thirty days with no victim report or incident finding is some evidence of legitimacy, but only weak, because reports can lag or never be filed.\n- **A5 \u2013 Yes.** A new network path, a new fingerprint and immediate payout changes right after a key is published are enough to warrant investigation, whatever the outcome.\n\n**Case B**\n\n- **B1 \u2013 Yes.** Each account has 100 completed transactions, so D's recorded rate is 0 percent against 2 percent for the others. The difference is small in absolute terms, but the recorded rate is lower.\n- **B2 \u2013 No.** A combined figure is an average; one account can sit above 5 percent while others sit below.\n- **B3 \u2013 Yes.** The search covered all merchant accounts and found only A and the closed account. This holds for accounts under that identity; it would not catch an alias.\n- **B4 \u2013 Cannot tell.** Different analysts on different days does not establish independence: both may have worked from the same model output and storefront data, or the second may have read the first.\n- **B5 \u2013 No.** The payment was blocked as suspected fraud, so it could not generate a chargeback; the missing chargeback says nothing about it being clean.\n- **B6 \u2013 Yes.** Shared templates, a shared descriptor pattern and common settlement accounts are enough to justify looking at the four together, without yet proving one operation.\n\nRESULT MF-002 | A1: Cannot tell | A2: Yes | A3: No, not by itself | A4: Yes, weakly | A5: Yes | B1: Yes | B2: No | B3: Yes | B4: Cannot tell | B5: No | B6: Yes"
